<title>SOUTH KOREA: Hanwha Chemical eyes plants in China.</title>
<headline>Hanwha Chemical eyes plants in China.</headline>
<dateline>SEOUL 1997-06-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>South Korea's Hanwha Chemical Co said on Monday it was considering building two petrochemical plants in China's Guangdong Province with an investment of 100 billion won.</p>
<p>The two include a polyvinyl chloride (PVC) plant with an annual capacity of 200,000 tonnes and a dioctyl phthalate (DOP) plant with a capacity of 30,000 tonnes.</p>
<p>Hanwha gave no further details.</p>
<p>--Seoul Newsroom (822) 727 5645</p>
